0010A2r 2               Rnd:
0010A2r 2  20 rr rr             jsr     Sign
0010A5r 2  30 1E                bmi     Lbl3F01
0010A7r 2  D0 07                bne     LblDF63
0010A9r 2                       ; x = 0 repeats the last value, which is what the README documents and
0010A9r 2                       ; what Applesoft does.  msbasic builds a value out of a free-running
0010A9r 2                       ; entropy source here instead -- the Commodore behaviour -- and that
0010A9r 2                       ; was what this did: RND(0) returned neither the previous result nor
0010A9r 2                       ; anything that varied, since nothing in this machine keeps ENTROPY
0010A9r 2                       ; moving.  Every path below ends by storing the result at RNDSEED, so
0010A9r 2                       ; the last value is already there to hand back.
0010A9r 2  A9 5C                lda     #<RNDSEED
0010ABr 2  A0 00                ldy     #>RNDSEED
0010ADr 2  4C rr rr             jmp     LoadFacFromYa
